In article <25siot$out@news.u.washington.edu> elskedar@stein2.u.washington.edu (Darren Eslke) writes:
>I have a cursed Platinum Exoress Card that I got from a magic lamp.
>It came that way, and I really want to fix it.  I have been hanging out

crom should be happy to give you some holy water.  Make some potions of
water by #dip'ing some useless potions into fountains, or dipping a unicorn
horn into certain "bad" potions.  

drop your potions of water onto your altar (probably a good idea to 
make sure they're all uncursed; cursed water can come in handy) and pray.

Crom will bless the potions, making holy water.  

You can then #dip the card into holy water twice, which will first
uncurse it  and then bless it.  Alternately, you can get a scroll of remove
curse from your favorite shop and read that (but be warned, if this
scroll is not blessed, it will uncurse a random cursed item in your pack). 
this will uncurse the card, you'll still need to use holy water to bless it.

other good items to bless:

luckstone:  number one.  bless this puppy, and good luck will never time
   out, but bad luck will
unicorn horn:  blessed unicorn horn, when applied, will cure all sorts of
   ills, all at once (ie: stunned, confused, sick, lost ability, etc). 
tinning kit:  makes blessed "pop-top" tins:  "this tin opens like magic"

not a bad idea to bless your rings and amulets and weapons and any tool
(pickaxe) that must be weilded, because if some monster curses one of these
items then you won't be able to take it off or unwield it.  Alternately, you
can just carry around a couple holy waters or scrolls of remove curse.  

